    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d150">

                <pb facs="0242" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A5 Submarines/18: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-08-15T14:00:00+01:00">August 15, 1936—2
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 15—9:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. My despatch 2423, August 6.<anchor n="4" xml:id="d150-f1"/> The Foreign
                    Office states that the French Government has now arranged to despatch its note
                    in connection with the submarine protocol on the 15th of August to the
                    diplomatic representatives in Paris of the agreements concerned. The date had
                    been postponed from August 10 to August 15 at British <pb facs="0243" n="163"
                        xml:id="pg163"/> suggestion to give the Italian Government further
                    opportunity to express its views on text of the protocol and general procedure.
                    The Italian Government not having replied, the British consider it impossible to
                    press the French to defer any longer the despatch of their note.</p>
                <p>The Italian Foreign Office has, however, advised the British Embassy in Rome that
                    it hopes shortly to deliver a favorable reply to the British representations in
                    connection with the submarine protocol.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bingham</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
